<title>BELGIUM: Belgian CCB cuts some bank certificate rates.</title>
<headline>Belgian CCB cuts some bank certificate rates.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian bank Credit Communal/Gemeentekrediet said on Thursday it would cut interest rates on some bank savings certificates from July 14.</p>
<p>    MATURITY	  NEW RATE	OLD RATE</p>
<p>    one year	  unchanged     3.00 pct</p>
<p>    two years	 3.30 pct	3.40 pct</p>
<p>    three years     3.65 pct	3.75 pct</p>
<p>    four years	4.00 pct	4.10 pct</p>
<p>    five years	4.35 pct	4.50 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - CCB is the Belgian market leader for bank savings certificates.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
